source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of (possibly non-commutative)\ngroups on <MATH_0003>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>pseudo torsor<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, or more precisely a\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>pseudo <MATH_0004>-torsor<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>, is a sheaf\nof sets <MATH_0005> on <MATH_0006> endowed with an action\n<MATH_0007> such that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> whenever <MATH_0008> is nonempty the action\n<MATH_0009>\nis simply transitive.\n<STRUCT_0003>\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0003>morphism of pseudo <MATH_0010>-torsors<TEXTITCLOSE_0003>\n<MATH_0011>\nis a morphism of sheaves of sets compatible with the\n<MATH_0012>-actions.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0004>torsor<TEXTITCLOSE_0004>, or more precisely a\n<TEXTITOPEN_0005><MATH_0013>-torsor<TEXTITCLOSE_0005>, is a pseudo <MATH_0014>-torsor such that\nin addition\n<STRUCT_0004>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(2)<ITEMCLOSE_0001> for every <MATH_0015>\nthere exists a covering <MATH_0016> of <MATH_0017>\nsuch that <MATH_0018> is nonempty for all <MATH_0019>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0006>morphism of <MATH_0020>-torsors<TEXTITCLOSE_0006> is a morphism of\npseudo <MATH_0021>-torsors.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0007>trivial <MATH_0022>-torsor<TEXTITCLOSE_0007>\nis the sheaf <MATH_0023> endowed with the obvious left\n<MATH_0024>-action.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b7019d1d91f558ed7f4e669b0521606b3222c284a3118000bc1cacfe244a5940", "unit_id": "tag:03AH:statement"}
